n: 3.6
name: fkwu-runtime
kind: hub
is: The old runtime fkwu is one C file of 34,149 lines built by one cc command in 3.7 to 8.5 s: an evaluator over 4-word code nodes with 256 tags, C and in-language emitters of AArch64 into MAP_JIT pages through one 20-line page allocation, an image cache, and 5,850 lines of host interfaces. fib(32) takes 0.54 s evaluated and about 0.05 s compiled. Its recorded faults sit where compiled and evaluated meaning differ. A 1,199-line carrier with no evaluator is in the tree; the reading estimates a C bootstrap of 1,400 to 1,600 lines.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.1
name: runtime
kind: hub
is: What the old runtime is: one C file of 34,149 lines that grew from 160 in five months while a banner bounds only its source-runner parser; a start through one large-stack thread and a 1 ms sampler; a value word classified by parity and magnitude; two node stores and a separate NodeID word; three unrelated uses of the words ice, water and gas; a moving pair collector beneath C code. The reading inferred from a text search that C holds no choice point and no trail: choice and undo are written in the language over one recover point.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.1.1
name: one-unit-one-command
kind: observation
is: The old runtime fkwu is one C translation unit, runtime/fkwu-uni.c, of 34,149 lines and 1,634,539 bytes, plus two generated headers of 37 and 302 lines. One command builds it: cc -O2 -o fkwu runtime/fkwu-uni.c. Its core is a tree-walking evaluator over code nodes of 4 words: a tag from 0 to 255 and three operands.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#561 2.1.7#665 2.9.2#14-16 2.1.10 2.1.11
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.1.2
name: boot-path
kind: observation
is: At start fkwu arms fatal-signal handlers, runs the evaluator on one thread with a 256 MB stack, and makes the first thread a sampler that wakes every 1 ms. Source in the higher grammar BML is lowered to Form text by a Form program of 23 units run as a cell inside the same process, with no pipe and no fork; the process then starts itself again.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#34114-34145 2.1.7#33187-33194 2.1.7#33988-34003
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.1.3
name: size-by-subsystem
kind: finding
is: The reading's division of the 34,149 lines of fkwu-uni.c: host interfaces (files, processes, sockets, HTTP, audio, camera) 5,850 or 17%; machine-code emitters in C 4,950; images and caches 4,800; shared-memory store 4,150; evaluator 3,900; reader 3,400; cell runs and diagnostics 3,350; values and memory 3,100; GPU interfaces 820.
status: inferred
from: 3.6.1.1
conf: mid
limit: Boundaries are approximate to about 150 lines per class; classes were assigned from function names and banner comments in 500-line windows.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.1.4
name: growth-under-bounded-banner
kind: observation
is: runtime/fkwu-uni.c had 160 lines at its first commit on 2026-06-28, 1,954 at commit 766519b6c of 2026-06-30, 13,647 before 2026-08-01, 25,570 before 2026-10-01 and 34,149 on 2026-11-24; 400 commits touch it. A banner calls its built-in source runner a one-time bootstrap and bounds that parser, not the file, against becoming a full C flattener.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#23277-23285
limit: 766519b6c (09:42 -0600) is the last commit before 2026-07-01 00:00 in the reading machine's zone, +0800. By the commits' own dates the last commit of 2026-06-30 is e394e1ac0 (16:50 -0600), with 1,977 lines.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.1.6
name: value-word-bands
kind: observation
is: A value in fkwu is one signed 64-bit word classified by parity and magnitude: even is a 63-bit integer; 1 is the empty list; odd positive indexes a pair; -8999999999999999999 is nothing; odd negative bands near -9e18, -8.5e18, -8e18 and -7e18 hold float boxes, strings, function values and records. Comments record two repairs of aliasing kinds.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#735-770 2.1.7#941-949 2.1.7#1640-1662 2.9.18#50-51
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.1.7
name: node-stores-and-node-word
kind: observation
is: Besides code nodes, fkwu keeps value nodes in column arrays addressed by index and interned by a hash of category and children, so the same category and children give the same node. A separate NodeID word has one mode bit, then either a 63-bit integer or package 6 bits, level 13, type 12 and instance 32.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#5649-5662 2.1.7#5758-5778 2.1.7#16944 2.1.11#6-14
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.1.9
name: memory-and-stops
kind: observation
is: In fkwu a copying collector compacts pairs at 90% fill and frees unreferenced strings in the same pass, so C code holding a pair or string index across a nested evaluation must push it first; a private note counts eleven branches repaired for held string indices. The float pool never reclaims a slot; a stop longjmps to the nearest recover point.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#6438-6446 2.1.7#9596 2.1.7#22953-22956 2.1.7#23613-23640
limit: Live strings never move: the string pass frees unmarked slots for reuse, and the hazard the note names is a freed slot, not a moved string.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.2
name: machine-code
kind: hub
is: How the old runtime makes and runs machine code: one 20-line page allocation shared by every emitter; two emitters in C of about 3,000 lines that start at a call count of 1,024; a 396-line emitter in the body's own language that starts at 4,096 and never receives what the C emitters took; a compiled function kept as a node of tag 194 with its original body as fallback; no page of these emitters saved to disk, while a document records native code on disk for two other paths written in the language.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.2.1
name: page-allocation
kind: observation
is: All fkwu emitters get executable memory from two C functions of 20 lines: mmap read-write-execute with MAP_JIT (0x1802 on Apple), pthread_jit_write_protect_np off and on around the copy, an instruction-cache clear; the carrier membrane-boot.c repeats it in 27 lines. A function from the C emitters gets one 16 KB page; others size it to their code.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#4905-4929 2.1.7#12330-12331 2.1.7#14435 2.1.7#10485-10492 2.1.7#5415-5430 2.1.7#5618 2.1.8#558-584
limit: The in-language emitter and the in-memory leaf map their code rounded up to whole host pages; the C leaf of tag 215 maps a fixed 4,096 bytes.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.2.2
name: c-emitters
kind: observation
is: Two emitters in C, about 3,000 lines of fkwu, write AArch64 words: one starts when a function has boxed 1,024 floats, the other at every 1,024th call of a function, closure calls excepted. Limits: 6 parameters (8 if all float), 24 slots, 8 string literals, up to four signatures; pages install only on Apple arm64, and a refusal is a numbered code.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#12313-12342 2.1.7#12367 2.1.7#12458-12479 2.1.7#2040-2044 2.1.7#14434-14463 2.1.7#14838-14844 2.1.7#10379 2.1.7#10403 2.1.7#15062-15065 2.1.7#14415 2.1.7#564-567 2.1.7#14967-14990 2.1.7#11083-11094 2.1.7#4883-4885 2.1.7#5600-5602
limit: The second emitter compiles a body with a self call as a loop and one without as a typed expression. The comment at 12475-12476 that only the first-seen signature is compiled is outdated. C holds a third emitter outside these 3,000 lines: for tag 215 it admits a small tree and emits a register-only image itself.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.2.3
name: tag-194-fallback
kind: observation
is: A compiled function stays in fkwu's function table as a tag-194 node holding its index and original body; its branch runs the page, or evaluates the body when no compiled signature matches. A body marked -1 is not asked again; a refusal coded below -1 reopens, at most 4 times, when a call's argument shape differs; a reload unmaps every page.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#12322-12326 2.1.7#11083-11094 2.1.7#15023-15046 2.1.7#14997-15019 2.1.7#12498-12511
limit: A function declined because a function it calls was not yet compiled is set back to unasked. The comment at 12325-12326 still says a declined body is never asked again; that holds for the mark -1 only.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.2.4
name: in-language-emitter-offer
kind: observation
is: A third emitter is written in the old body's own language: jit-page.bml, 396 lines. When a function's call count reaches a multiple of 4,096, or its sampler hits a multiple of 32, fkwu offers the function to that program as a cell in the same process and binds the AArch64 words returned. The offer skips a function the C emitters already compiled.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#10227-10231 2.1.7#10281 2.1.7#10296-10300 2.1.7#31791-31801 2.1.14
limit: The reading counted the emitter's lines and read the C side; it did not read the emitter's body and could not run this path, so no speed figure exists for it.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.2.5
name: page-helper-table
kind: observation
is: A page from fkwu's in-language emitter is called with a table of 38 words: the value stack, a continue-at node, six C helpers, 26 operations and four frame words. The layout's number, 4, goes with every offer; an emitter written for another number declines. The page keeps values in the evaluator's frame, where the collector sees them.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#10233-10279
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.2.6
name: machine-code-not-saved
kind: observation
is: Pages from the emitters of 3.6.2.2 and 3.6.2.4 are not saved: the old body's document says emitted words contain current function and node indices and literal-pool words, so saving raw pages is insufficient, and every process emits again. It records native code on disk for two in-language paths: the scalar demand JIT and compiled GPU programs.
status: observed
src: 2.9.3#48-53 2.9.3#73-87 2.9.3#109-113 2.1.7#27808
limit: The on-disk image, format version 9, stores the evaluator's node graph. The scalar path selects 'a current disk image' and keeps 'a SHA-256 sealed admission'; one .metalbin 'contains the native archive'. Both are read from the document; neither path was run for this node.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.3
name: measures-and-records
kind: hub
is: Timings the reading took on one machine, and what the old body's documents and private notes record: a build of 3.7 to 8.5 s; fib(32) at 0.54 s evaluated and about 0.05 s compiled, with a 2.2 to 4.0 s spread on one evaluated loop; an image 645 times its source because the cache unit is the whole closure; image identity from content with a 64-bit key; eight copies of each primitive; two recorded cases of compiled code changing meaning near the 1,024th call.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.3.1
name: build-and-startup
kind: finding
is: On an Apple M4 Max with Apple clang 17.0.0 on 2026-11-24, cc -O2 built fkwu-uni.c at commit b8ff978c9 in 3.7 to 8.5 s across runs into a binary of 745,624 bytes with the linker's ad-hoc signature and no entitlements. In the reading's runs it ran machine code in MAP_JIT pages, and a process evaluating (add 40 2) from source ended in 10 to 11 ms.
status: assumed
limit: One machine. The 8.5 s (8.2 s user) is the reading's single build at load average 3.6 and did not repeat: three rebuilds in the review round took 3.67 to 3.87 s wall (3.6 to 3.7 s user) at load average 4.4. The MAP_JIT run and the start time are the reading's own and were not repeated. A private note of 2026-11-09 records 3.6 s and 711 KB for the file of that day. Whether a hardened-runtime or notarized build needs the allow-jit entitlement was not tested.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.3.3
name: closure-image-645-times
kind: observation
is: A document of the old body, measured 2026-11-13: a 59,464-byte unit became 201,998 bytes of lowered text and a 38,391,347-byte image, 645 times its source, because its closure of 351 units is assembled whole. A cold build cost 0.37 s per MiB of image. The document says one edit invalidates a whole closure while the unit of meaning is the recipe.
status: observed
src: 2.9.4#5-8
limit: The figures are the document's own measurements; the reading did not repeat them.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.3.4
name: cache-identities
kind: observation
is: fkwu stores its binary under a digest of three source files and build flags, with a SHA-256 seal checked before use; a comment says builds of one version are byte-identical when file name and layout are fixed. An image's identity binds the builder, the unit's path, and the paths, sizes and digests of its closure; the store key is 64-bit FNV-1a.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#33691-33710 2.1.7#28246-28262 2.9.3#58-66
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.3.6
name: compiled-code-changed-meaning
kind: finding
is: Two private notes record compiled code in fkwu differing from evaluated code. 2026-10-03: past 1,024 calls an inlining step dropped the effects of arguments the callee did not read; 3,936 of 780,000 effects happened. 2026-11-24: a closure over locals stopped with a wrong error at about its 1,024th call; the note says the fault is not repaired.
status: assumed
limit: Read as records; the reading reproduced neither fault.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.3.7
name: primitive-copies-drift
kind: finding
is: The reading lists eight places one fkwu primitive is written: evaluator branch, operation function, C emitter, page slot, mirror table, image arity table, flattener row, manifest row. Private notes record two drifts: a node field past the arity table kept pointing into the first image's nodes; in the retired Go kernel a compiled len undid a repair.
status: assumed
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.4
name: carrier-and-bootstrap
kind: hub
is: The carrier already in the old tree and the reading's bootstrap estimate. membrane-boot.c, 1,199 lines, has a word of 0, 1, nothing or node, immutable cells identified by canonical bytes, offer as its only act and no evaluator; its end-to-end proof runs cc on the 34,149-line old runtime. The reading weighs three forms of stored compiler, estimates 1,400 to 1,600 lines of C for an evaluator over stored numeric cells, and concludes for C.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.4.1
name: carrier-word-and-acks
kind: observation
is: The carrier membrane-boot.c defines a 64-bit word: 0 is state 0, 1 is state 1, 2 is nothing, (slot<<2)|3 is a node. Offer is its only act, acknowledged by one of those four. Held work is not a word: offer sets arrived=0 and writes no ack. A timeout is an arrived nothing. An unoffered interface acknowledges state 0 and records a breach row.
status: observed
src: 2.1.9#10-29
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.6.4.2
name: carrier-cells-leaves-proof
kind: observation
is: In the carrier membrane-boot.c a cell is immutable; its identity is the canonical bytes of kind, children and payload, and a digest only indexes the store. Its C evaluates no recipe and has no arithmetic: a leaf is machine code the image supplies. Limits: 8,192 cells, 32 children, one page per leaf. Its proof runs cc on the 34,149-line fkwu-uni.c.
status: observed
src: 2.1.9#17-37 2.1.8#22-26 2.1.8#562 2.9.7#1-12 2.9.19#449-453
at: 2026-11-24

